  "Heart of Darkness is the indispensable European text about empire and one of the founding works of modern fiction: it invented the colonial journey narrative that the century would find endless uses for, gave the language 'the horror', and its technique — the framed narrator, the delayed disclosure, the symbolic river — made Marlow the model for the modern unreliable narrator. Chinua Achebe's attack on it in 1977 made it the centre of the debate about the colonial canon, which is itself part of its record.",
